35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,- **Daisuke**: The logs show eleven misroutes from duplicate addresses. The coordination group is just two people writing everything by hand.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Daisuke, that confirms my fear. Two people doing the work of ten. The vendor logs show the same certificate requested repeatedly.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the rollout data is damning. Half the plants lose signal daily, and approval took six weeks. We promised dates on blind faith.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the capital line is frozen. Only the recurring software allowance has room. Per-head licences climb with every department added.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, my data matches. Broad tools died, narrow ones survived. We keep funding the wrong shape.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the duplicate addresses are a data problem, not a people problem. We need to fix the records, not just add staff.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, fixing records is good, but who does the manual entry? The two clerks are already drowning.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, frozen capital kills anything needing hardware. We must pick a project that fits the recurring software allowance, or it dies in the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, exactly. Per-head licences are a trap. We need a fixed-fee model to avoid the renewal bill.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, fixed-fee is safer, but my standardization data shows four of six efforts died without an owner. We need a clear champion, not just a contract.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, you are right. The manual entry is the bottleneck. I worry the new project will just add to their existing load.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, exactly. If we pick a project that needs more manual coordination, those two people will break. We need something that reduces their load, not adds to it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, agreed. But the real killer is the six-week approval lag. If the groundwork isn't verified before we start, we are just setting a new trap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the approval lag is a symptom. The real risk is the per-head licence climbing next year. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, the standardization record shows narrow tools survive. We need a project with a single, clear owner to avoid the ghost projects.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I am quiet. I just want to ensure the next project does not add to the two clerks' burden.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,I am done. The data is clear.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
